# Deformation Problems, Chapter 2: Examples of deformation problems

The source section is an editorial list of topics that should eventually be
developed: deformations of schemes (including the Rim--Schlessinger
condition, tangent spaces, infinitesimal deformations, and affine
hypersurfaces), deformations of quasi-coherent sheaves, deformations of
algebraic spaces, and deformations of maps.  It contains no precise
mathematical definition, hypothesis, assertion, identity, diagram, exact
sequence, or worked example.  Consequently this section contributes no Lean
declarations.
